      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “middle class” as people with “moderate financial means”; it only states that the asylum is for “private patients of the middle class” and gives payment ranges (e.g., sums varying from “los. to £2 a week”).",
        "While the packet supports that these were “private patients” who paid (“all of whom pay, for their medical treatment and maintenance”), it does not directly state that this is what defines the term “middle class” (the definition’s wording treats this as definitional).",
